Nethack is the most popular hack-n-slash ascii game around, and Doom is the
most popular hack-n-slash 3-D game around.  Don't the two just seem to go
naturally together?  Actually I don't think it would be that big of a leap
to combine the two, putting the adventure of a D&D-type game into the 3-D
realism of Doom's animation.  You'd have to add a few new things to Doom
but constructing the levels in 3-D shouldn't be that hard.  I think it might
be easier to convert Nethack into a Doom-type interface than to convert Doom
into a Nethack-type game.

So now the question I'd love to hear answered "yes":  is anyone out there
working on such a beast?  Email me.
